<!--
  Status-bar icon: the full Bounce mark as a flat white silhouette.

  All three shapes are here on purpose. An earlier version dropped the green fan
  on the theory that overlapping white shapes would merge into a blob at 24dp,
  which left a visibly incomplete mark. They do not merge: the gap between the
  fan and the wave in the logo is genuine empty space between two non-touching
  paths, not a white shape painted on top, so the union reads correctly. This
  matches ui/assets/adaptive_icon.png, the white silhouette the Fyne build passed
  to setSmallIcon.

  This drawable is used in two places that render it very differently: the
  status bar draws it small and white in a 24dp box, and from Android 12 the
  notification shade draws it tinted inside a *circular badge*, which is the
  large colour icon beside the app name.

  These two pull in opposite directions, and the size below is a deliberate
  choice between them rather than a spec value.

  The status bar wants the Material system-icon grid: a 24dp box with an 18dp
  keyline for a square mark, which is what other apps fill and what makes their
  icons look right. At 62.5% (15dp) this mark was visibly smaller than its
  neighbours.

  The Android 12 badge wants the opposite. Measuring the real ink rather than the
  bounding box - the furthest path point from the centre of the 24dp box, which
  is where the badge's inscribed circle is centred:

      62.5% (15.01dp)  ink reaches  9.84dp  = 82% of the 12dp badge radius
      75.0% (18.00dp)  ink reaches 11.81dp  = 98%   <- touching the mask edge
      83.3% (20.00dp)  ink reaches 13.12dp  = 109%  <- clipped

  So the 18dp keyline is unusable here: it puts the mark hard against the badge
  mask, which is the same "reads as cropped" failure an earlier 72.4% version
  had. 75% is not a coincidence - 0.724*24 = 17.4dp is essentially the same size.

  68.8% (16.5dp) is the compromise: ink at 90% of the badge radius, so the mark
  still floats inside the circle, while being 10% larger in the status bar than
  the version that looked undersized.

  scale  = (24 * 0.688) / 400 = 0.04122
  offset = (24 - 16.50) / 2 = 3.761 across, (24 - 15.74) / 2 = 4.129 down
-->
